{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Normally, Rule 12d1-4 requires:\n\n- **Acquiring fund adviser:** Evaluate the structure’s complexity and aggregate fees and expenses, and find that the acquiring fund’s fees and expenses do not duplicate the acquired fund’s.\n- **Acquired fund adviser:** Find that undue-influence concerns are reasonably addressed, considering the investment’s scale and maximum limits, anticipated redemption timing, potential in-kind redemptions, and agreement terms.\n- **Board reporting:** Each adviser reports its evaluation, findings, and rationale to its fund’s board by the next regularly scheduled meeting.\n- **Written interfund agreement:** Before exceeding statutory limits, include material terms supporting those findings, termination by either fund on no more than 60 days’ written notice, and the acquired fund’s obligation to supply reasonably requested fee-and-expense information.\n\n**Worth knowing:** The agreement generally is unnecessary when both funds have the same investment adviser; that exception does not eliminate the required adviser findings."}}
